<%# One turn in the transcript. Local: debate_turn. Rendered on first paint and
    appended in place by debate_turns/create.turbo_stream.erb (local-time re-processes
    stream-inserted <time> nodes automatically).

    `dom_id(debate_turn)` on the row is LOAD-BEARING and not decoration: the synchronous
    controller response and the async `broadcast_append_later_to` both append this same
    turn, and Turbo's id dedup is the only reason the second append is a no-op instead
    of a duplicate row. It is also what spec/system/debate_phases_spec.rb scopes its
    phase assertions to. Never render this partial without it.

    CHAT BUBBLE (Hoojah 2026, redesign Phase 3, Task 3.4) — mockup ~1123-1134. The
    transcript's own `flex flex-col` stack (`_debate_transcript`) is what lets a bubble
    align itself with a plain `self-start`/`self-end`, no extra wrapping row: `side` is
    derived from `debate_turn.user_id == debate.challenger_id`, and it drives BOTH the
    alignment and the corner that stays square (the "tail"), same as any chat UI.

    THIS DELIBERATELY OVERRIDES the design system's byline-only rule —
    docs/design-system/components/debate/DebateTurn.prompt.md says "There is no stance
    border, no side label and no arrow — the byline is the only indication of who is
    speaking," and Slice 9 Task 4.5 built exactly that. The 2026 redesign supersedes it
    for this one surface: bubble alignment already tells the two participants apart
    spatially, and the mockup adds a THIRD signal, a speaker-stance-coloured "Phase ·
    @handle" micro-label, on top of it. The colour is the same agree/disagree
    challenger/opponent convention `_debate_pending` and `_debate_scoreboard` use for
    this trio — not `IconsHelper#stance_color` / `Hujah::STANCES`, which colour a claim
    VOTE elsewhere in the app. Do not read this override as license to colour any other
    `ui/_card`-based row by its author; it is scoped to this one component because a
    debate has exactly two speakers and the mockup asks for it explicitly.

    The avatar stays — Slice 9 Task 4.5's `ui/_avatar` (`size: :sm`) — and its `alt`/
    `aria-label` fallback stays the reason spec/models/debate_broadcast_spec.rb's
    "no photo" example is safe: `photo` is nullable and `image_tag nil` raises, which is
    reachable on the broadcast path where nobody sees the exception. Do not drop the
    avatar chasing the mockup's spacing — that spec asserts its `aria-label` fallback by
    name.

    `.debate-turn-phase` stays scoped to ONLY the phase word (not "Phase · @handle" as a
    whole) — spec/system/debate_phases_spec.rb anchors an exact regex
    (`/\A#{label}\z/i`) against that class alone, so folding the handle into the same
    element would break every phase assertion in that file.

    Locals: debate_turn, debate. `debate` is a SEPARATE local rather than
    `debate_turn.debate` on purpose: `belongs_to :debate` is not eager-loaded on the
    `@turns` collection (only `:user` is, in `DebatesController#show`), so reaching for
    it here would issue one extra query per turn in the transcript — a fresh N+1 this
    partial did not have before. Every call site (the transcript collection render, the
    create Turbo Stream, and `Debate#post_turn`'s broadcast) already has the debate in
    hand and passes it through instead. %>
<% side = (debate_turn.user_id == debate.challenger_id) ? :challenger : :opponent %>
<div id="<%= dom_id(debate_turn) %>"
     class="debate-turn shadow px-3.5 py-3 max-w-[86%] <%= "debate-turn-enter" if local_assigns[:entering] %> <%= (side == :challenger) ? "self-start rounded-2xl rounded-bl-md bg-card" : "self-end rounded-2xl rounded-br-md bg-disagree-soft" %>">
  <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 mb-1 min-w-0 <%= "flex-row-reverse" if side == :opponent %>">
    <%= render layout: "ui/user_link", locals: {user: debate_turn.user, class: "shrink-0"} do %>
      <%= render "ui/avatar", user: debate_turn.user, size: :sm %>
    <% end %>
    <span class="text-[10.5px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wide truncate <%= (side == :challenger) ? "text-agree" : "text-disagree" %>">
      <span class="debate-turn-phase"><%= debate_turn.phase_label %></span>
      <span class="mx-1">·</span> <%= render layout: "ui/user_link", locals: {user: debate_turn.user, class: (side == :challenger) ? "text-agree" : "text-disagree"} do %>@<%= debate_turn.user.username %><% end %>
    </span>
  </div>
  <div class="hujah-body text-sm text-ink break-words"><%= format_body(debate_turn.body) %></div>
</div>
